{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76775-deep-ones-as-cryptids","id":76775,"title":"Deep Ones as Cryptids?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-21T18:58:18-08:00","id":76775,"title":"Deep Ones as Cryptids?","content":"I know, roll your eyes. H.P. Lovecraft, overdone, Cthulhu, yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> In terms of species like the Mothmen or Reptilians, Cryptids strike me as a fascinatingly weird part of the nWoD to play with. Considering they seem to be all sorts of shades of weird, they seem like a pretty good catch-all origin for some strange monsters.<br /> <br /> Then I got thinking about one of my favorite little monster groups, the Deep Ones from the Mythos, and they struck me as a decent idea for Cryptids. They'd be sneaky, making habitats under the sea. They're secretive and prefer to go unchallenged and so they tend to hide out near isolated human communities. What if they still need humans to reproduce? The bargain might be doing weird things with Aether or some abandoned Infrastructure in the depths to produce valuable items or something for people, while in exchange they help the Deep Ones proliferate?<br /> <br /> Maybe this version they're sort of shapeshifters. They look like the Deep One Hybrids before they change usually, but they shift into Full Deep One mode when threatened/exposed to water.<br /> <br /> I don't think Cthulhu is needed here at all. Maybe there's a greater cryptid named Dagon or something that's the progenitor of them. They make weird cities really far down in the depths of the world's oceans.<br /> <br /> Maybe some Demons exploit them as minions, or maybe there's even one or two enterprising demons who have tried to make one of their deep cities into their own personal Hell.<br /> <br /> Spitballing ideas here of Deep Ones as cryptids. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:10:39-08:00","id":76789,"title":"","content":"I think two things:<br /> <br /> 1) My Deep One itch is mostly already scratched by the Brineborn from War Against the Pure.<br /> 2) &quot;Tempter Does Rapture with Fish-Cryptids&quot; feels like a thing that I need to make a Cipher or three in service of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T21:48:53-08:00","id":76861,"title":"","content":"Throughout human history, The God-Machine has seen the need to occasionally experiment on humanity. Quiet knocks on the door in the middle of the night answered by people who were never seen by their communities again. Rarely does this happen en masse but occasionally, the God-Machine sees the need to use a section of humanity for specific purpose. On the months of October 1909, November 1920, and April 1934, the God-Machine saw it fit abduct nine small communities through out the world and subject them to a campaign of genetic engineering and mental conditioning. The purpose of this was gain a supply of labor to construct and maintain Infrastructure on the sea floor. Brainwashed via Angels and GM cults, the new &quot;Deep Ones&quot; are now bent to servicing the Infrastructure that they maintain on the sea floor (to the point where they even worship parts of it with names as &quot;Father Dagon&quot; and &quot;Mother Hydra&quot;).<br /> <br /> The towns themselves are thoroughly enthralled in the cults of the God-Machine and always watched by at least one Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 02-22-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T15:18:51-08:00","id":77355,"title":"","content":"I think the God Machine is ripe for Cthulhu-esque horrors and stuff. Hell, angels as described in sort of a Lovecraftian way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:50:11-08:00","id":80577,"title":"","content":"Aaand I'm off to read some Lovecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:01:42-08:00","id":80585,"title":"","content":"An odd bit of Infrastructure tucked away in a reef off the coast of a small fishing village causes the local fish and fishermen to meet in the middle? Yeah, I can see it. And then VALKYRIE comes along (or takes the credit for a small group of decidedly &quot;green&quot; sorts) and bombs the reef, leaving the remaining Deep Ones to wander off, looking for new Aether in all sorts of weird places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:02:24-08:00","id":80630,"title":"","content":"Read my mind. There could be a significant piece of Command infrastructure tucked away in some bizarre, cyclopean facility at the bottom of the sea, broadcasting messages to angels and stigmatics in the form of strange dreams... Just saying!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:06:47-08:00","id":80632,"title":"","content":"A Tempter considers the old axiom &quot;If you can't beat them, join them.&quot;. He certainly doesn't want to rejoin the God Machine, but perhaps one can work like it, in some ways at least? Make ones own foot soldiers, build ones own machines and constructs to help things, keep them separate, make sure not to lose more than one at a time...<br /> But, where could one hide such things? Something meant to grow large will eventually be Noticed, after which it is obvious what will come. The cleanse.<br /> Then again... the sea floor, yes, there are no machines, no useful pawns there, no reason for It to even pay attention...<br /> <br /> And hence, over centuries, the Cult grew, built machines, fed it's God with sacrifices, to keep it in this world. Soon, in a few years, they will launch their efforts onto land, make their strike against the oppressor, the Machine, and the world will be free!<br /> <br /> (or so they think)<br /> And that was how the God Machine suddenly found itself in a strange and, to it, confusing war. Lots of unknowns coming out of nowhere, sometimes with tech that Shouldn't Exist, and most importantly of all, recruiting the Fallen, even MAKING some fall... how did it come to that?<br /> Or perhaps it was how a certain Demon built his own hell, then when he passed his kingdom went mad, starting to Do Things. One could twist it in so many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:24:35-08:00","id":80644,"title":"","content":"That's a fascinating plot right there: a Demon has realized his Cipher and achieved Hell for himself... and it's mucking things up for everyone else. Reality is starting to glitch in the immediate area (Splinters bleeding together? You betcha!), the Machine is in a full alert &quot;damage control&quot; mode, and the mortals are getting curious. You need to shut up or shut down (ha!) one of your own who hasn't done anything wrong; is this the fate waiting for all of you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}